  "composer": {
    "accepted_prose": "Mia paused, the dish towel held still against her palms as she considered his question with a small, careful nod. \"The counter near the stove—I'm using it to set out some things I need,\" she said, her voice gentle but practical. \"It would help if that spot stays clear. The rest is fine, though you're welcome to stay nearby if you like.\"\n\nShe glanced toward the open kitchen, then back at him, her tone a shade warmer. \"I don't mind the company,\" she added, \"as long as you're not in the way. I mean—of the work. The hot work. Not you.\" A faint, self-conscious laugh escaped her, and she looked down, smoothing the towel.\n\n\"So… a little corner is yours,\" she finished, her expression settling into cautious warmth. \"But I'm not going to tell you where to stand. You can decide what feels right.\"",
